# SOUNDNESS FIXTURE — the self-host lowerer must evaluate the BASE of an
# `&<projection>` call argument EXACTLY ONCE, even when a downstream predicate
# (`field_storage_holds_pointer` for a pointer-storage field, an unknown inner
# type, an unresolved field name) declines the write-place resolution.
#
# CLASS: `amp_object_base` (self_host_lowerer/lower_expr.gg) used to fall
# through to `lower_place_base` for a call/arithmetic/method-result base,
# which BOTTOMS OUT in `lower_expr(base)` — the base's side effects were
# emitted, then the write-place resolver declined on a downstream predicate,
# and the `&`-argument chokepoint re-lowered the WHOLE argument
# (`lower_expr(arg)`), evaluating the base a SECOND time. The fold restricts
# `amp_object_base` to place-shape whitelist (EIdentifier / ESelfExpr /
# EDeref / EFieldAccess / EIndex), returning None for other shapes so the
# fallback path lowers the argument exactly once. Mirrors the `_ => None`
# arm of Rust's `place_expr_type_only` (src/ir/lowering/exprs/mod.rs, around
# the `Postcondition 2 — EMISSION` comment).
#
# SAMPLED CELL (Core #12): a CALL as the projection base whose declared
# return type carries an OPAQUE-HANDLE field (RWLock — reads `true` from
# `is_opaque_pointer_type` in self_host_lowerer/lir_lower.gg, so
# `field_storage_holds_pointer` fires and `lower_amp_place` declines). The
# base `mk()` prints `MK` — a visible side effect. A single call site
# reaches every `&<projection>` face; other bases (a bare local, a nested
# projection, an index) are exercised by cow_amp_field_arg / …_type_axis /
# …_deref_box_projection.
#
# GUARDED MECHANISM: the whitelist arm of `amp_object_base`. Restore the
# `else` arm to `lower_place_base(base_expr, gmod)` (or remove the `return
# None`) and the base's `mk()` fires TWICE.
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the pre-fix self-host (Track D commit 30d5f60d):
#   MK
#   MK
#   look
#   done
# Rust gg (oracle) and the post-fix self-host both print:
#   MK
#   look
#   done
#
# The `look` callee is intentionally read-only through its `&`-parameter —
# the fixture pins BASE EVALUATION COUNT, not write-through behaviour (which
# is pinned by cow_amp_field_arg).
from std.sync import RWLock

struct Config:
    int port

struct Bag:
    RWLock[Config] lock

Bag mk():
    print("MK")
    return Bag(RWLock[Config](Config(10)))

void look(RWLock[Config] &l):
    print("look")

void main():
    look(&mk().lock)
    print("done")
